{
 "_readme": "TRACK segments for the map wizard (Palle 2026-07-24: 'x 13 width and as long as needed in z... template maps as a starting point... concatenate... then bring in the order... add related artifacts'). Each segment is a 13-wide x 7-deep template map in the /template-maps role grammar (template_patterns.json), extended: '' void, '1' walk floor, 's' spawn, '1s' walk slot, 'r' room floor, 'rs' room slot, 'y' yard floor, 'ys' yard slot (anti), 'm' moat void, 'p' parapet h2, '2' raised, '3' lowered wall h3, '4' wall h4, 't' teleporter void. Seam rule: rows z0/z6 hold only walk or void so any two segments concatenate walkably. slots carry cap (max artifact body cells, FIT law at slot). The engine (tools/wizard_compose.py, track mode) concatenates a plan of segments along z, pours the order into slots walk-order, and kin-fills leftover slots with registry-category relatives. Segments may have ANY depth (rows count) — the engine stacks cumulatively; hall_grand is 13 deep.",
